	<http://sbols.org/v3#description> "Recombinase XerC of the XerCD complex." ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#description> "Xer C is activated by a septum-translocated FtsK at cell division. It pairs with XerD to make an activated complex which cleaves or inverts sequences at dif-sites, depending on dif-site directionality. See Edinburgh project 2007 for details.\n\nIt turns out that XerC overexpression is a very effective way of not getting any colonies on your agar-plates. Therefore the Edinburgh 2007 team never incorperated it into its final construct." ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#author> "Caroline Dahl" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#source> "XerC is an innate E. coli K12 locus." ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#created> "2007-10-22T06:00:00.000Z" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#note> "The coding XerC sequence contains none of the restriction sites used when biobricking." ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#status> "Planning" ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#type> <https://identifiers.org/SBO:0000251> ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#hasSequence> <http://parts.igem.org/Part:BBa_I742134#sequence> .
