	<http://sbols.org/v3#name> "BBa_I742133" ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#description> "CrtIB genes with PstI site mutated out" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#description> "CrtIB encodes two enzymes, which make up steps three and two in the carotenoid biosynthesis pathway respectively.\n\nCrtI encodes phytoene desaturase and CrtB encodes Phytoene synthase.\n\nBoth cloned genes still have their native ribosome binding sites.\n\nMore information about the carotenoid synthesis pathway may be found on the [http://parts.mit.edu/igem07/index.php/Edinburgh/Yoghurt/Design#Colour_Production Edinburgh Yoghurt Wiki]" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#author> "sarah hollingshead" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#source> "Genes were both isolated from Pantoea ananatis (formerly Erwinia uredovora) \nDSMZ 30080, ATCC 19321\n\nDiversity of Carotenoid Synthesis Gene Clusters from Environmental Enterobacteriaceae Strains, N Sedkova, APPLIED AND ENVIRONMENTAL MICROBIOLOGY, 71(12): 8141???8146 (2005) \n\nElucidation of Pathway the Erwinia uredovora Carotenoid Biosynthetic by Functional Analysis of Gene Products Expressed in Escherichia coli, N Misawa, et al, JOURNAL OF BACTERIOLOGY, 172(12): 6704-6712 (1990)" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#created> "2007-10-22T06:00:00.000Z" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#note> "The CrtI gene contained two PstI sites, which were both mutated out using point mutagenesis" ;
	<http://parts.igem.org/#status> "Planning" ;
	<http://sbols.org/v3#type> <https://identifiers.org/SBO:0000251> .
